## Hints for Future Agents
Disable hooks per invocation for local commits and merges: the repository's post-commit hook automatically pushes master and can rebase it. Herdr treats keys.json as the complete keymap, so the file includes the other macOS defaults. Herdr does not automatically add new defaults after a personal keymap is installed. Custom mods open the built-in worktree dialog with the active space, focused terminal folder, and action new or open; the built-in dialog handles remote machines. Herdr-generated gpui-kit.d.ts and jsconfig.json files appear inside the symlinked mod directories and are intentionally ignored. The active symlinks now point into the main checkout. The feature worktree and branch remain available but are no longer needed by the installed configuration.

## Codebase Discoveries
The TUI uses configs/herdr/config.toml and the desktop uses ~/.config/herdr-app/keys.json. They do not share configuration. The installed app has mod.open but no direct worktree creation or opening commands, so each shortcut needs a helper mod. Custom directory mods work through symlinks. The dedicated installer honors HERDR_APP_HOME, backs up a regular keys.json, and uses the existing link_tree helper for mod directories.

